#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Maida: Calabria, 4 July 1806.  A sample game for the Grognard engine.

A small British army, landed three days before in the bay of Sant'
Eufemia, meets Reynier's French on the plain below the hill town of
Maida.  French columns come on against a British line: the textbook
fight of line against column.  Play either side against the computer,
or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./maida (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.maida.json.  ./maida --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

